      "title": "Carpenter/Painter",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nJob Summary: Responsible for performing all aspects of carpentry work, including finish carpentry, building and repairing furniture, and framing with wood and metal studs. Key Results and Responsibilities Ability to perform window and glass repair Ability to work off ladders and scaffolding Ability to repair and/or install doors, door hardware, and locks Ability to repair and/or install various roofing systems Ability to repair and/or install masonry work Ability to exercise proper care and cleaning of tools and worksites Responsible for following through on assigned work orders Must be able to work occasional off-hours to complete projects Moving furniture, fixtures, and equipment as necessary Duties may involve snow shoveling on occasion May be assigned to assist and/or perform painter's duties along with carpentry work Other duties as may be assigned and/or necessary Required Qualifications Five or more years as a professional carpenter Knowledgeable in all aspects of carpentry work Knowledge of painting Knowledge of sanding, staining, and refinishing woodwork Lifting ability Good attendance is necessary Physical Demands & Working Conditions The physical demands described below are representative of those required to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform these essential functions: Mobility:  This position requires the ability to perform maintenance tasks, including climbing stairs, ladders, and catwalks. Lifting and Carrying:  The role involves lifting and carrying objects, with a maximum weight of up to 50 pounds. Vision:  The ability to read printed materials and view information on a computer screen is necessary. Hearing and Communication:  The job requires effective communication skills, including the ability to hear and speak clearly in person and over the telephone. Working Conditions: The working environment may include exposure to various conditions: Environmental Exposure:  The work involves moving between indoor and outdoor environments, which may result in exposure to varying weather conditions and abrupt temperature changes. Biohazards and Chemicals:  Employees may encounter biohazards and hazardous chemicals as part of their duties. Confined Spaces and Heights:  The job may require working in confined spaces and at heights. Note:  The employer is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities, enabling them to perform the essential functions of the job in a safe and effective manner.",
