    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f49f191a-7524-465b-8442-e0768f85867a&ccId=31713375_2&jobId=45771513_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "IT Endpoint Systems Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\n\nThe approximate base compensation range is posted, but the actual offer will reflect our total compensation and benefits package. The offer will be determined by a number of factors including the selected candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, FTE, number of months worked, as well as internal equity among our team. Position Summary: The IT Endpoint Systems Engineer is an innovative problem solver responsible for the expert-level administration of the college’s endpoint ecosystem. This role focuses on designing and automating complex endpoint lifecycles using SCCM, JAMF, and Entra/Azure ID to support the evolving needs of our community. The ideal candidate is a specialist in Apple and Windows deployment and enterprise print management, ensuring mission-critical user environments are optimized, secure, and accessible Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Endpoint Lifecycle Management: Lead the design, implementation, and maintenance of automated OS deployment and software packaging using Microsoft SCCM and JAMF Pro for both Windows and Apple environments Identity & Cloud Access: Serve with Identity Access Team in Entra ID (Azure AD), managing cloud-based identity, conditional access, and integration within the Microsoft 365 ecosystem\\ Advanced Print Management: Architect and manage the college’s enterprise print environment, specifically leveraging Papercut to ensure secure, efficient, and audited print services across all campuses Apple Ecosystem Expertise: Act as the subject matter expert for all Apple hardware and iOS/macOS management, ensuring seamless integration and configuration via JAMF Automation & Scripting: Craft advanced PowerShell and Shell scripts to automate routine endpoint tasks, reducing manual intervention and improving system analytics Proactive Monitoring: Configure and manage specialized monitoring systems for computer and printer endpoints to identify issues and implement proactive solutions Platform Server Maintenance: Maintain the health, security, and performance of server environments hosting critical endpoint management systems, including SCCM, JAMF, and Papercut; perform regular OS patching, software version upgrades, and performance tuning to ensure 100% service availability Security & Compliance: Ensure all endpoints remain compliant with security policies through rigorous patching processes via SCCM, Intune, and JAMF Technical Documentation: Create and maintain high-level documentation for endpoint configurations, print workflows, and deployment procedures to empower junior IT staff Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree in information technology, or related field AND five (5) years of professional systems support experience; OR an equivalent combination of education, training, and experience. Skills and Competencies: Expert-level proficiency in Microsoft SCCM and JAMF Pro for large-scale enterprise environments In-depth knowledge of Entra (Azure AD), including user management, group policies, and cloud-based security Specialized expertise in Apple hardware (Mac, iPad, iPhone) and the macOS/iOS operating systems Advanced experience managing enterprise print solutions, specifically Papercut MF/NG Strong scripting skills in PowerShell or similar languages for system administration, reporting, and automation. Experience with Microsoft Intune and modern desktop management practices Proven expertise in the management, security, and maintenance of Windows Server environments specifically hosting mission-critical endpoint and print management platforms (such as SCCM, JAMF, and Papercut) Understanding of LAN principles specifically as they pertain to the security and deployment of computer and printer endpoints Preferred Qualifications: Relevant professional certifications, such as JAMF Certified Admin, Microsoft Certified: Endpoint Administrator Associate, or Apple Certified Support Professional Previous experience in Higher Education managing diverse student and faculty endpoint needs Expertise in Papercut administration and print server optimization Physical Requirements: Mobility to work in a typical office setting and use standard office equipment. Vision to read printed materials and a computer screen. Hearing and speech to communicate in person or over the telephone. Strength to lift and carry up to 20 pounds. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Work Environment: Schedule: Full-time, on-site position (Monday–Friday, occasional evenings/weekends required for major system implementations or critical incident resolution) Additional Duties: Occasional participation in school events, meetings, and extracurricular activities as required. Disclaimer: This job description is not intended to be an exhaustive list of all duties, responsibilities, or qualifications associated with the position. Duties may be added, removed, or modified at any time to meet the evolving needs of the college.   #Ll-JG1",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=f49f191a-7524-465b-8442-e0768f85867a&ccId=31713375_2&jobId=50951544_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Maintenance Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\n\nThe approximate base compensation range is posted, but the actual offer will reflect our total compensation and benefits package. The offer will be determined by a number of factors including the selected candidate’s experience, knowledge, skills, abilities, FTE, number of months worked, as well as internal equity among our team. Salary: $85,000-$92,000 Position Summary: Manage and supervise maintenance functions in the Facilities Services Department. Provide project management services on various projects. Required Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in engineering or combination of education, work experience or equivalent.  In depth knowledge of the following areas: Building trades and general maintenance Steam plant operations, Refrigeration systems, General safety practices as related to maintenance OSHA requirements Computerized preventative maintenance programs Electrical, mechanical, and utility distribution systems Experience in project management  Required Knowledge and Skills Knowledge of: Administrative principles and practices, including goal setting, program development, implementation and evaluation, and the supervision of employees Principles and practices of developing teams, motivating employees and managing in a team environment Materials, methods, practices and equipment used in facilities construction, maintenance and repair Principles and practices of budget development and administration Building utility, mechanical, HVAC systems and steam plant operations principles and practices Federal, state and local laws, codes, regulations and policies Principles, practices and methods of construction management Vendor and contractor management and oversight Computer applications related to the facilities management field Techniques for dealing with a variety of individuals from various socioeconomic, ethnic and cultural backgrounds  Working experience in project management A proven ability to plan and schedule work and establish priorities Ability to select, train and supervise skilled trades This job description lists the major duties and requirements of the job and is not all-inclusive. Incumbent(s) may be expected to perform job-related duties other than those contained in this document and may be required to have specific job-related knowledge and skills. Ability to hire, direct, and manage architects, engineers, and design professionals Experience in developing and managing annual operating and capital budgets Mobility to work in a typical office and construction settings and use standard office equipment, vision to read printed materials and a computer screen; stamina to negotiate rough terrain, climb, crawl and stoop; hearing and speech to communicate in person or over the telephone; strength to lift and carry up to 50 pounds Work is subject to travel, exposure to adverse environmental conditions, hazardous chemicals, fumes, dust and noise Willingness and ability to to work extended and/or off-hours as needed. Provide response on urgent and emergency off-hours issues. Participate in scheduled rotation for weekend/holiday manager-on-duty program Skilled in: Planning, organizing, supervising, reviewing and evaluating the work of others Developing and implementing goals, objectives, policies, procedures, work and safety standards Communicating effectively in oral and written forms Supervising a variety of construction, remodeling, maintenance and repair programs and activities Developing effective work teams and motivating individuals to meet goals and objectives and provide customer services in the most cost effective and efficient manner Interpreting, applying and explaining state and local laws, codes, regulations and policies Exercising sound independent judgment within general procedural guidelines Building, equipment and mechanical system troubleshooting Assessing and prioritizing multiple tasks, projects and demands Contributing effectively to the accomplishment of team or work unit goals, objectives and activities Establishing and maintaining effective work relationships with coworkers and students Essential Functions: Plans, organizes, administers, reviews and evaluates the work of assigned staff and students Recommends selection of staff; trains staff and provides for their professional development; administers discipline as required Develops and implements goals, objectives, policies, procedures and work standards for the unit; prepares and administers the unit's budget Manages, schedules and oversees preventative maintenance programs for both College and Monastery equipment, buildings and mechanical systems; assigns and schedules daily preventative maintenance work orders to minimize equipment failures; schedules equipment downtime if necessary and coordinatewith effected CSS and Monastery staff; reviews building equipment manuals and manufacture data for recommended preventive maintenance needs as well as service intervals; develops task sheets to be entered as PM work orders into the TMA system; monitors equipment failures and analyzes needs for improvements to PM system; adjusts service interval frequencies when needed and researches new service products which may extend the service interval, energy efficiency or equipment life span This job description lists the major duties and requirements of the job and is not all-inclusive. Incumbent(s) may be expected to perform job-related duties other than those contained in this document and may be required to have specific job-related knowledge and skills Arranges for and manages service contracts; provides specifications and contractor responsibilities to be included in proposals; reviews cost and expected performance standards; manages and negotiates service contract extensions Assists with management of construction projects; oversees contractors and staff; develops and maintains standards for equipment and materials and ensures standards are met Estimates equipment, materials and staff required to perform assigned projects; requisitions supplies and equipment and maintains an inventory of regularly used materials Represents the department and the College and acts a liaison with other departments and representatives of other organizations and agencies; participates on a variety of task forces and committees; oversees the best interests of the College in the areas of service provision and resource utilization Responds to and resolves staff inquiries and complaints Directs the conduct of and conducts analytical studies and planning efforts; acts as the College’s expert resource in areas of responsibility; develops and reviews reports of findings, alternatives and recommendations; directs the maintenance of accurate records and files Performs inspections of facilities to ensure safety and maintenance; inspects work performed to ensure adherence to established service standards and specifications Contributes to the efficiency and effectiveness of the department's service to its customers by offering suggestions and directing or participating as an active member of a work team   Physical Demands & Work Environment:  The physical demands described herein are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of the job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.",
